# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# Playwright (spec 22) — generated auth state and run artifacts, never committed.
/playwright/.auth/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/

# next.js
/.next/
/.next-e2e/
/out/

# production
/build
/dist

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Terraform (infra/terraform) — .terraform/ is a regenerated local cache of
# downloaded provider binaries (hundreds of MB, architecture-specific);
# never commit it. .terraform.lock.hcl (the version pin) is committed
# deliberately, unlike the directory above. environments/dev/terraform.tfstate
# is committed deliberately (see that file's own main.tf) — a single-operator
# sandbox account with no remote state backend. Spec 23: production and the
# bootstrap config that creates production's remote-state backend are the
# opposite — their state must never be committed (production's normally
# lives only in the S3 backend and never touches disk; the bootstrap
# config's local state is the one exception this repo still uses locally,
# and the owner is responsible for backing it up outside git — see
# progress-tracker.md's spec 23 entry).
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate.backup
infra/terraform/environments/production/terraform.tfstate
infra/terraform/bootstrap/terraform.tfstate
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
